    "text": {
     "en": "The modern age began with the Renaissance, a rebirth of art and learning in Europe from the 14th century. Artists like Leonardo da Vinci and Michelangelo and thinkers like Galileo changed how people saw the world.\nPrinting with movable type by Gutenberg spread knowledge. The Reformation, led by Martin Luther, questioned the Church. The Age of Discovery sent Columbus to America and Vasco da Gama to India in 1498.\nThe new sea routes opened trade and led to colonies. Voyages brought wealth but also hardship for native peoples."
    }
